# Opening a dialog announces its title, then the control focus lands on.
#
# Reported on hardware: "when the settings window opens and the first thing it
# lands on is the settings categories, nothing is read."
#
# The title is a Now-priority announcement, and Now used to drop every pending
# lower-priority item — including the announcement of where the user actually
# was. Interrupting is the point of Now; deleting the user's place is not.

node title  Window   "Aura Settings"
node first  ListItem "General" pos=1 size=7
say "Aura Settings"
focus first

expect
  Aura Settings
  General, list item, 1 of 7
